2) Output ONLY the issues you actually find. Do NOT list categories that are already fully passed.
3) For every finding, provide:
   - Category name
   - Severity (Blocker / High / Medium / Low)
   - File path + line number(s)
   - Exact risky snippet (short)
   - Why it violates WP.org guidelines
   - The correct WordPress-compliant fix (with a minimal code example)
   - Any related secondary risks (security/performance)

Plugin context you can rely on:
- Plugin slug/permalink (WordPress.org): [PASTE_PLUGIN_SLUG_HERE]
